  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Postfix % coerces to a number, divides by 100, and flushes subnormal quotients to +0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, the postfix percentage operator (x%) coerces its scalar operand to a number, divides by 100 using Excel's division arithmetic, and flushes any subnormal result to +0 (so 1E-307% gives 0 rather than 1E-309).",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in jnt_operators (rows 12 and 20) and dc_e00t (row 5).",
